    "title": "Texas vs. Purdue final score, results: Purdue rallies past Texas for Elite Eight",
    "text": "Texas vs. Purdue final score, results: Purdue rallies past Texas for Elite Eight originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.Texas entered the night as a No. 11 seed, while Purdue stood as the No. 2 seed. Sean Miller has led the Texas Longhorns to the Sweet 16 in his first season in Austin. What started as a first four in Dayton led the Longhorns to become the lowest-seeded team remaining in the NCAA tournament. They have upset NC State, BYU, and Gonzaga. It’s only the second time in 2008 that the Longhorns have advanced this far.AdvertisementBut it was Purdue who had the last word with a 77-77 tie.Purdue stood as the No. 2 seed, backed by head coach Matt Painter and a squad that has reached the tournament three times in a row at the regional semifinals. The Boilermakers are Big Ten tournament champions, defeating the Michigan Wolverines, 82-70.They'll now advance to take on Arizona or Arkansas.Texas vs. Purdue live updates, results, highlights from Sweet 16FINAL: PURDUE 78 -- TEXAS 778:29 PM -- MARCH MADNESS MOMENT -- TIED UP 77-77. 8:18 PM -- The final minute of regulation has begun. Purdue holds a narrow 73-72 lead over the Longhorns.Advertisement8:11 PM: With just under 3 minutes left, Purdue holds a narrow 72-70 lead over Texas.7:54 PM -- Just under eight minutes remain in San Jose, and the Texas Longhorns are holding a narrow 65-63 lead.7:52 PM -- Texas holds a close lead, 61-60.7:40 PM -- Foul reviews delayed much of the first five minutes. Texas challenged and was denied, losing a timeout. Texas holds a narrow lead, 49-47.7:19 PM -- SECOND HALF TIPOFF-- Winner advances to the Elite Eight, taking on Arizona or Arkansas.6:57 PM -- HALF -- Purdue 37 -- Texas 35 6:56 PM -- Texas and Purdue head into the final minute with just a two-point trail by Texas, 37-35, Purdue.Advertisement6:35 PM Chendall Weaver is having a field day for Texas.6:35 PM -- It's a close game in San Jose. Tramon Mark leads the Longhorns with 12 points, while Trey Kaufman-Renn has 8 points and 4 rebounds.Attending the Sweet 16 matchup in San Jose is Texas Football head coach Steve Sarkisian.Texas vs. Purdue start timeDate: Thursday, March 26Time: 7:10 p.m. ETThe NCAA tournament game between Purdue and Texas is set to tip off at 7:10 p.m. ET from the SAP Center in San Jose, Calif.What channel is Texas vs. Purdue on today?TV channel: CBSPurdue vs. Texas will air on CBS. Brian Anderson and Jim Jackson will be on the call, and Allie LaForce will serve as the sideline reporter.AdvertisementFans can stream the game live on Fubo, which offers a free trial for new subscribers so you can try the service before you buy.Stream ESPN, ABC, CBS, Fox and 100-plus top channels of live TV and sports without cable. (Participating plans only. Taxes and fees may apply.)Paramount+ is another streaming option for all CBS games in the tournament.",
